editorialMd:
Build windowMaxes

Take every group of exactly `k` numbers next to each other in `readings`. Move the group one place right each time. Record the largest number in each group, from left to right. If `k` is larger than the input length, `windowMaxes` is empty.

Return the answer

Find the largest number in `windowMaxes`. Store it in `largest`. Complete `windowPegsPeakTicket` so it returns `largest`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `windowMaxes` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

javascript
function windowPegsPeakTicket(readings, k) {
  const a=readings; let out=[];
  const queue=[];let head=0;for(let i=0;i<a.length;i++){while(head<queue.length&&queue[head]<=i-k)head++;while(head<queue.length&&a[queue[queue.length-1]]<=a[i])queue.pop();queue.push(i);if(i>=k-1)out.push(a[queue[head]]);}
  let answer=out.length?out[0]:0;for(const x of out)if(x>answer)answer=x;return answer;
}


